---
import PathwayLandingLayout from '../../layouts/PathwayLandingLayout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '@/lib/seo/config';
import { TEA_INVESTMENT_THRESHOLD } from '@/lib/eb5-investment';
import { getPathwayHero } from '@/lib/pathwayHeroes';

const title = 'EB-5 Visa for Chinese Investors: A 2026 Guide | StudentEB5';
const metaDescription =
  'EB-5 for Chinese investors covers investment requirements, visa category considerations, I-526E filing, and project selection for Chinese nationals in 2026.';
const canonicalUrl = `${SITE_CONFIG.url}/pathways/eb5-for-chinese-investors`;
const h1 = 'EB-5 Visa for Chinese Investors: A 2026 Guide for Chinese Nationals';
const subhead =
  'What Chinese nationals need to know about investment requirements, visa category timing, and the filing process before pursuing an EB-5 green card.';

const teaFormatted = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {
  style: 'currency',
  currency: 'USD',
  maximumFractionDigits: 0,
}).format(TEA_INVESTMENT_THRESHOLD);

const relatedResearch = [
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Cryptocurrency Source of Funds',
    url: '/research/eb5-cryptocurrency-source-of-funds',
    description: 'Documenting crypto origin, liquidation, and path of funds for EB-5 petitions.',
  },
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Projects Without I-956F: Due Diligence',
    url: '/research/evaluating-eb5-projects-pending-i956f',
    description: 'What to review when a project has not yet received I-956F approval.',
  },
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Immigrant Investor Program: Complete Guide',
    url: '/research/complete-2027-eb5-guide',
    description: 'Filing steps, rural set-asides, and current program structure overview.',
  },
];

const hero = getPathwayHero('eb5-for-chinese-investors');
---

<PathwayLandingLayout
  title={title}
  metaDescription={metaDescription}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  h1={h1}
  subhead={subhead}
  relatedResearch={relatedResearch}
  secondaryCtaText="Talk to Someone Who Understands EB-5 for Chinese Investors"
  breadcrumbTitle="EB-5 for Chinese Investors"
  heroImage={hero.image}
  heroImageWebp={hero.webp}
  heroImageAlt="EB-5 pathway for Chinese investors"
  keywords={[
    'EB-5 for Chinese investors',
    'EB-5 China 2026',
    'Chinese nationals EB-5',
    'EB-5 visa China',
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="extraCompliance">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed border border-border rounded-lg bg-secondary/40 p-4 m-0">
      EB-5 investment involves financial risk, including potential loss of principal, and does not guarantee a green
      card, visa availability, or any specific processing time. Consult a qualified immigration attorney and a
      FINRA-registered financial adviser for guidance specific to your situation.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <p>
    The EB-5 Immigrant Investor Program gives eligible foreign nationals a path to a U.S. green card through a
    qualifying investment. Chinese nationals have historically made up one of the largest investor groups in the
    program's history, and the program's rules, including visa category availability, reserved categories, and filing
    requirements, apply specifically based on country of birth. This guide covers what Chinese investors need to
    evaluate before filing.
  </p>

  <h2>Investment requirements</h2>
  <p>
    EB-5 requires a qualifying investment in a new commercial enterprise, structured to create the required number of
    U.S. jobs. Most investors use the reduced Targeted Employment Area (TEA) investment threshold of {teaFormatted}
    rather than the standard amount. See our full
    <a href="/research/eb5-economic-calculus-investment-cost">EB-5 Investment Cost breakdown</a> for current figures.
  </p>

  <h2>Visa category and timing: what "country of birth" means for Chinese investors</h2>
  <p>
    EB-5 visa numbers are allocated by country of birth (chargeability), not current citizenship or residence.
    Chinese-born investors have historically experienced longer visa category wait times than investors born in most
    other countries, due to per-country limits and demand. Reserved visa categories, including rural and infrastructure
    projects, were created partly to address this by setting aside a portion of visa numbers outside the standard
    queue. This is a complex, frequently changing area of the program; investors should review current
    <a
      href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/legal/visa-law0/visa-bulletin.html"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Visa Bulletin</a
    > data and discuss their specific timeline with an immigration attorney rather than relying on general estimates. For
    program structure context, see the
    <a href="/research/complete-2027-eb5-guide">complete EB-5 guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The filing process, in brief</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Select a project and complete source-of-funds documentation</li>
    <li>
      File Form I-526E (with concurrent adjustment of status filing for investors already in the U.S. on a valid
      nonimmigrant status, or consular processing for investors abroad)
    </li>
    <li>Receive work authorization and travel document during the concurrent filing period, where applicable</li>
    <li>Await visa number availability and I-526E adjudication</li>
    <li>File Form I-829 to remove conditions on permanent residence</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    For the full step-by-step guide, see the
    <a href="/eb5-investment-process">EB-5 investment process</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Choosing a project</h2>
  <p>
    Project selection is one of the most consequential decisions in the EB-5 process. Regional centers with USCIS
    I-956F approval have had their compliance and job-creation methodology reviewed by USCIS, which is one factor (not the only factor) in evaluating a project. See our
    <a href="/research/19-questions-rural-eb5-project-due-diligence">due diligence guide</a> and
    <a href="/research/choosing-rural-eb5-regional-center-guide">rural EB-5 regional center guide</a> for the fuller list
    of questions to ask before committing capital.
  </p>

  <h2>For students and families</h2>
  <div class="not-prose grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
    <a
      href="/pathways/eb5-for-chinese-students"
      class="block rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-6 hover:border-primary hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-150"
    >
      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-2">EB-5 for Chinese International Students</h3>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed m-0" style="line-height: 1.75;">
        If you're currently on F-1 status and evaluating EB-5 as an alternative to the H-1B path, start here.
      </p>
    </a>
    <a
      href="/pathways/eb5-for-chinese-families"
      class="block rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-6 hover:border-primary hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-150"
    >
      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-2">EB-5 for Chinese Families</h3>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed m-0" style="line-height: 1.75;">
        If a parent or family member may be funding the investment, see how the gift and source-of-funds process
        typically works.
      </p>
    </a>
  </div>
</PathwayLandingLayout>
